      "id": "OQ-1",
      "q": "B-3b88's own CHK-002 lets its implementer satisfy 'stop refresh_stale from re-certifying pass without re-execution' via EITHER (a) re-executing the command and refreshing only on continued pass, OR (b) refusing to refresh result:pass rows outright. B-1507's plan assumes B-3b88 only ships the interim self-contradiction/demote behavior and that B-1507's CHK-002 is the sole owner of refresh re-execution. If B-3b88's implementer picks option (a), the two in-flight stories both implement re-execution on the same refresh_stale function -- which owns it, and should B-3b88's checklist be narrowed to option (b) only to keep the coordination additive rather than duplicative/conflicting?",
      "evidence": "B-3b88 checklist.json CHK-002 context: 'Either re-execute the row's command and refresh only on continued pass, or refuse to refresh result:pass rows and require real re-verification; make the documented (rerun command) semantics honest.' vs. B-1507 understanding.json constraints: 'Coordinate ADDITIVELY with B-3b88 (interim per-row laundering guard) which edits the same refresh_stale function -- do not revert or conflict with its per-row self-contradiction guard' (which frames B-3b88's refresh_stale touch as only the demote/self-contradiction interim, not re-execution).",
      "sourcePointers": [
